    { version = "2.1.0", text = "Two new looks: Forever Style unit frames on Blizzard's own frame plate, and FlareUI Style party and boss frames with the portrait ring.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffFrame style|r (Unit Frames > Look) has three choices: |cffffffffFlareUI|r (the bronze ring beside FlareUI's bars, the default), |cffffffffForever|r (new) and |cffffffffAddon|r (plain frames). Each style keeps its own setup: sizes, positions, totems, and the party and boss frames.\n• Forever Style: the player, target and focus frames on Blizzard's Forever frame plate, with its name box, health and power slots and the bronze ring. |cffffffffScale|r in Edit Mode sizes the frame in Blizzard's proportions, Width stretches it. The name sits in the name box, the health and power texts in the middle of their bars.\n• FlareUI Style: the |cffffffffparty and boss frames get the portrait ring|r. Party frames: the player frame's ring and level disc, the role icon where the PvP crest sits, the leader crown and raid marker on the ring, the ready check and summon / resurrect / phase icons on the portrait. Boss frames: the target frame's ring and level disc (a skull for ?? bosses) with Blizzard's elite, boss and rare frames. Both have |cffffffffPortrait Size|r. Raid-Style party frames stay as they are.\n• |cffffffffFlareUI Forever|r bar texture: Blizzard's Forever health bar art, now the default for every bar (unit, party, raid, boss and resource bars, every cast bar, the XP bar). Absorbs keep FlareUI Striped.\n• Party Frames: |cffffffffDispel Icons|r is a switch and sits on the portrait: up to four, two to a row (in the middle of the health bar on frames without a portrait).\n• Damage Meter: a |cffffffffHeader|r font in the Fonts tab, for the title row (Damage Meter or Threat, the session and its timer).\n• XP Bar: |cffffffffBar Texture|r.\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffPvP Timer|r in Addon Style too, |cffffffffShow Level|r on every frame, |cffffffffHide Auras|r on the focus frame.\n• Boss Frames: |cffffffffMirror|r and |cffffffffOnly My Debuffs|r (both on by default), and |cffffffffAbsorb Texture|r.\n• Edit Mode: sample incoming heals and shields on the unit frames, sample aura timers, and portraits on the party and boss samples.\n• The Target, Focus and Pet Edit Mode dialogs have the \"FlareUI settings\" button too.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Each style has its own defaults for the player, target, focus, pet, totems, party and boss frames: sizes and positions to fit its look.\n• Classic combo points follow the style: always on in FlareUI and Forever Style, off in Addon Style (the option is gone).\n• Party and boss auras above or below the frame fit as many to a row as the frame's width allows, as the unit frames' auras do. Auras above or below any frame sit closer to it.\n• Aura size: 18 on the focus frame, 24 on the player and target frames, by default.\n• Incoming heals use the frame's bar texture. Shields always grow back from the end of the bar (Absorb Reverse Fill is gone).\n• The dispel highlight colours the frame's own border.\n• Party, boss and raid frames show no timers on auras inside the frame.\n• Unit Frames page: Colour palette sits under Frame style; Hide Player and Pet is now |cffffffffFade Player and Pet|r.\n• Party Frames: Party Targets is now |cffffffffShow Party Targets|r and Pets |cffffffffShow Pets|r; Spacing sits under Orientation; Target Gap is gone (fixed); Portrait sits above Health Text; Dispel Highlight above Dispel Icons (raid frames too).\n• Raid Frames: Spacing and Group Spacing moved to the Raid section, under Groups.\n• Icons: Raid Target is now |cffffffffRaid Markers|r.\n• Only My Debuffs is no longer on the player frame. Power Bar for Healers Only is gone: party and raid frames show everyone's power when Power Bar Height is above 0.\n• The PvP timer sits right beside the PvP crest.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Minimap: the addon button bag no longer takes in Questie's quest markers (or other addons' map pins), which stretched it down the screen.\n• Damage Meter: the bar font reaches every row, group members joining later included." },
